  "notes": "No motif on Satan's footsteps (168, negated). Footsteps (170) are the forefathers' tracks they follow. STAGING v4: 168-169: people sit to eat of the lawful good things of a garden (wheat plate, ended before the Name) and shake their heads at evil; Satan and his footsteps are never drawn. 170: the believers advise (Al-Muyassar: قال المؤمنون ناصحين) and the misguided refuse, turning to their forefathers' tracks (footsteps plate). 171: the caller keeps calling (As-Sa'di: دعاء الداعي) while they do not hear; the shepherd and the animals of the parable are not drawn."
